  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On rue Jean Aicard in Sainte-Maxime, Le Carillon describes itself on its official website as a "pizzeria and wood-fired grill in the old village, on a large, cosy and welcoming terrace". The site lists traditional cuisine, sea view, air conditioning, private hire, terrace and wifi; payment by card, holiday vouchers, meal vouchers or cash. The business has been registered at Fréjus since February 2019 and is still active according to Infogreffe. It opens daily from 12pm to 2pm and from 7pm to 10pm.</p>
      <p>The food is praised on several independent platforms: 4.8/5 on Restaurant Guru (1,127 reviews), 96% recommended on its Facebook page (44 reviews) and 4.0/5 on Tripadvisor (about 380 reviews), where travellers mention the wood-fired fish and the pizzas while others complain about slow service or the welcome on some summer evenings.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The official website (restaurantlecarillon.fr, read on 14/11/2026) does not list "pets allowed" among its services, and no rule about dogs was found from an official source (the restaurant or the tourist office). Several customer reviews describe a warm welcome for dogs, with one account even mentioning a chair offered for a small dog: a good sign, not a guarantee.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask for a terrace table when you arrive — that's where your dog will be most comfortable.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is in the old village of Sainte-Maxime, on rue Jean Aicard, and according to its website the terrace has a sea view; the seafront and town centre are close by.</p>
    </div>

